--- /dev/null
+++ b/Ghostgram/Features/ProfileExport/Sources/FakeGifts/LOCAL_PURCHASE_VERIFICATION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+# Native local purchase verification
+
+Not compiled or run on a simulator in this Windows environment. The existing production
+source glob includes every `.swift` below `Sources`, so XCTest files must be added to a
+separate test target rather than placed alongside these sources.
+
+On macOS, build the full Telegram target using the root CLAUDE.md command, then verify:
+
+1. With Fake Gifts enabled and this account's simulation toggle enabled, enter the normal
+   market Buy/Gift flow, select another user, add a caption and confirm. Test Stars with
+   zero balance and TON with zero balance: no top-up screen and no purchase/transfer RPC.
+   Observe the existing sticker success overlay and confetti; no real chat service message
+   is created. Check the recipient's Gifts tab even when their server gift count is zero.
+2. Verify model, pattern, backdrop, number and caption; unique owner and original recipient
+   must be the selected user. Own-profile gift list must not contain that recipient's gift.
+3. Restart the app and verify the gift persists. Switch to a second account and verify it
+   does not see the first account's copies or simulation setting. Returning restores them.
+4. Disable simulation after entering confirmation, then confirm: transaction stays local.
+   Disable the main Fake Gifts toggle during confirmation: the local transaction is saved
+   but hidden until it is enabled again. Neither change may trigger a payment fallback.
+5. Cancel at message/confirmation screens: no new record. Disable simulation before a new
+   flow: normal Telegram payment behavior remains; do not confirm a real transaction in
+   this test unless intended. Price-change and top-up retries retain their captured route.
+6. Make the account's fake-gifts.json parent unwritable and confirm a local purchase: show
+   failure, no success animation, no new in-memory gift, no payment RPC. Restore permission
+   and retry. Corrupt or unknown-version files must not be overwritten.
+7. Load a version-1 file with recipientPeer absent: old records remain on the own profile.
+   Add a recipient gift and confirm every old record remains after restart. A legacy import
+   must remain available if writing the new file fails.
+8. Leave a local gift screen open and disable both toggles. Try stale sell, transfer, wear,
+   craft, upgrade, original-detail removal, conversion and offer actions: no server mutation.
+   Hide/show works through the local hook; delete remains available in the local editor/menu.
+9. Record native UI transitions using the root AGENTS.md frame workflow. Inspect clipping,
+   recipient navigation, gift sticker playback and confetti; report frame references.
+
+Media references use the existing MediaBox cache. Restart persistence is covered; availability
+of animation files after clearing that cache is not guaranteed. The outgoing server-message
+gift animation cannot occur without a real message; success uses the existing local UI effects.
